# Build context for container/Dockerfile is the repository root, so this file
# lives here rather than in container/.
#
# Keeping node_modules out is not just about image size: the host's tree may
# have been installed for a different platform or Node version, and copying it
# in would shadow the clean `npm ci` the Dockerfile performs.

node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.github
.netlify

# Secrets must never enter an image layer, where they persist even if a later
# layer deletes them.
.env
**/.env
*.keystore
*.jks

*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Local tooling and docs that the running site does not need.
.claude
docs
DEPLOY.md
TWA.md
twa-manifest.json
deno.lock

# The sellable product package is not part of the running storefront; it is
# embedded into netlify/lib/site-audit-source.mts at authoring time.
packages

Dockerfile
container/.env

# Builds and publishes the image; it has no job inside one.
container/image.sh
container/ci
